; RFC 8610's `eb64url` expected-conversion prelude tag in MEMBER position. It expands to
; `#6.21(any)`: a nominal tagged-`AnyCbor` wrapper that retains the fixed CBOR tag around an arbitrary
; payload. It is advice for a consumer rendering the item, not a base64 API invented by the generated
; crate. `eb64legacy` (#6.22) and `eb16` (#6.23) use the same shared representation with their own
; fixed tags; `cbor-any` (#6.55799(any)) is deliberately different and remains permanently refused,
; because it self-describes an entire serialized CBOR stream rather than an ordinary value.
;
; This catalog row executes the member path in a fresh process, catching a regression to a graceful
; rejection or an abort. The exact default/preserve tag codecs, all three siblings, and the wider
; name-resolution product are pinned by
; `expected_conversion_prelude_tags_generate_and_emit_exact_tags_in_every_position` and
; `expected_conversion_preludes_generate_through_every_supported_name_resolution_context`
; (src/tests/robustness_tests.rs and src/tests/refused_name_closure_tests.rs).
a = [v: eb64url, x: uint]
